{"title":"Make All K-Window XORs Zero","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given an array `a` of `n` non-negative integers and a window length `k`. In one operation you choose any index `i` and replace `a[i]` with **any** non-negative integer.\n\nFind the minimum number of operations needed so that every contiguous subarray of length `k` has bitwise XOR equal to `0`.\n\nAll original elements are smaller than `2^6 = 64`.","inputFormat":"The first line contains two integers `n` and `k`.\nThe second line contains `n` integers `a[0], a[1], ..., a[n-1]`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the minimum number of operations.","constraints":["1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 1000","0 ≤ a[i] < 2^6"],"examples":[{"input":"4 4\n1 2 4 8","output":"1","explanation":"There is a single window and its XOR is 15. Changing the last element from 8 to 7 makes the XOR of 1, 2, 4, 7 equal to 0, and one operation is clearly needed."},{"input":"5 2\n1 2 1 2 1","output":"2","explanation":"Two adjacent elements have XOR 0 only if they are equal, and windows overlap, so all elements must become equal. Turning the two `2`s into `1` costs 2 operations."},{"input":"6 3\n1 2 3 1 2 3","output":"0","explanation":"Every window of length 3 is a rotation of 1, 2, 3 and 1 ^ 2 ^ 3 = 0, so nothing has to change."}],"tests":[{"input":"1 1\n5","output":"1"},{"input":"1 1\n0","output":"0"},{"input":"4 2\n0 0 0 0","output":"0"},{"input":"3 3\n63 63 63","output":"1"},{"input":"3 3\n1 2 3","output":"0"},{"input":"5 1\n7 7 7 7 7","output":"5"},{"input":"15 3\n3 7 0 7 1 2 0 5 3 1 3 6 1 3 3","output":"10"},{"input":"5 1\n0 0 1 1 1","output":"3"},{"input":"9 1\n11 40 26 11 6 26 58 27 59","output":"9"},{"input":"11 1\n2 1 0 5 1 3 1 6 3 0 6","output":"9"},{"input":"18 3\n16 20 51 50 26 23 36 61 45 58 53 58 56 30 27 2 2 25","output":"15"},{"input":"3 3\n2 1 0","output":"1"},{"input":"4 3\n3 3 1 2","output":"1"},{"input":"1 1\n4","output":"1"},{"input":"15 3\n28 48 61 42 28 56 11 34 60 62 14 10 48 48 49","output":"12"},{"input":